<refentry id="gmime-contents">
  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>MIME part content</refentrytitle>
    <refmiscinfo>GMime Library</refmiscinfo>
  </refmeta>

  <refnamediv>
    <refname>MIME part content</refname>
    <refpurpose>Read or copy a MIME part's content with GMimeContent</refpurpose>
  </refnamediv>
  <refsect1 id="data-wrapper-overview">
    <title>Reading and copying content</title>

    <para>A <type>GMimeContent</type> object holds a stream and its content
    transfer encoding. Use <function>g_mime_content_open()</function> to
    read decoded bytes without making a full copy, or
    <function>g_mime_content_decode_to_stream()</function> to write the
    decoded bytes to another stream. To copy the original bytes without
    decoding them, use <function>g_mime_content_write_to_stream()</function>.</para>
  </refsect1>
</refentry>
